  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Location and Physical Character
    
    The Hearth Plaza occupies the southern reaches of Aurora Stack near The Still Pools, a stagnant corruption site whose proximity the original architect either did not foresee or did not consider disqualifying. The plaza is built around vertical crystal spires engineered to channel aurora-light into the interior galleries. Approximately half these galleries are now sealed with opaque ice. The remaining open sections still luminesce, though the rhythm is irregular — a stutter rather than the steady pulse described in Clever Ice Age records. In the affected sealed zones, temperature holds at precisely negative seventy-three and a half degrees regardless of season. That figure appears in three independent assessments. I would normally distrust such agreement, but the thermal ice-memory corroborates it.
    
    ## Design
    
    Light-Regent Xouhoulong, the Aurora Stack leader who consolidated power through The Icebound Exchange during the Faction Wars, designed the plaza during the Clever Ice Age as a neutral meeting ground between Aurora surface-dwellers and Nightshelf tunnel-dwellers. The trade-floors are arranged in concentric rings, each level originally assigned to a different guild, the whole structure engineered to funnel sky-light downward into the deepest market tiers.
    
    The upper galleries still function largely as Xouhoulong intended, each crystal spire angled to paint occupants in shifting blue and violet. A central dais, tilted six degrees off true north toward the Nightshelf tunnels — a diplomatic gesture encoded in architecture — allows the presiding authority to address council sessions. An eastern archway serves formal delegation entrances. Behind the dais sits an antechamber scaled for private negotiation: small enough that two penguins cannot avoid each other, large enough that a third could overhear through the wall. The crystal geometry funnels sound as effectively as light, a property designed for oratory that proved equally effective at carrying Wake-Singer hymns through the spires during the Orca Incursion.
    
    ## History of Control
    
    The plaza's chain of custody tells the story of Aurora Stack's instability more concisely than any political history:
    
    | **Period** | **Controlling Entity** | **Notes** |
    |---|---|---|
    | Clever Ice Age | Light-Regent Xouhoulong | Original construction; Xouhoulong displaced after the Calving and the exposure of his secret research programs |
    | Post-Calving | The Wake-Singers (orca shaman cult) | Occupied during a period the chronicles treat with understandable revulsion; burn-scarring throughout the ice dates to attempted cleansing of this occupation |
    | Faction Wars era | Holdborn (ice-thresh) | The war associated with this splinter faction left corruption staining the ice itself |
    | Present | The Icebound Exchange | Commercial operations restored; fire-core shipments transit on schedule; trade conducted in three dialects |
    
    Despite the Exchange's commercial dominance, the plaza remains listed as the sole territorial holding of Holdborn (ice-thresh) in the Stack's factional registry — a faction whose broader properties and membership have been, in the Council's phrasing, "revised sharply downward." Locals call the plaza "the Scar" when they think no one official is listening. Xouhoulong's memorial stands untended. Someone scratched initials into its base. A single fire-core left there as offering has fused into the ice.
    
    ## Anomalous Features
    
    The southern gallery was sealed following a cascade event in which an artifact designated R5-X6XN6VK9, a Void Matrix stored at the plaza, consumed aurora-light from the surrounding environment for six hours. When light returned, it refused to enter that section. The aurora simply will not touch it. During the Long Dark, ancestral manifestations appear in the trade galleries — some apparently browsing the stalls, their purposes unreadable. High-Beak Auditor Selka, an Exchange official killed during the great Calving, manifested as a translucent form from the plaza wall and observed the living for three hours before the veil reclaimed her.
    
    ## The Sealed Galleries
    
    Beneath the trade-floors, in chambers Xouhoulong sealed before the first merchant entered, spiral channels were carved into ancient ice. Fire-core braziers maintained precise temperatures for research into deep-ice pressure-magic — research Xouhoulong authorized secretly under the doctrine of Mandatum∴absconditu while publicly maintaining the plaza as a site of open diplomacy. The experiments drew a response. The spiral channels began to self-extend, carving paths in directions no one had planned. Two researchers vanished when the ice breached spontaneously. The channels continued reaching toward the deep tunnels. They have not stopped.
    
    The corruption vectors designated ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral and Shawl☽ Sun are both documented as active within the plaza's ice. Whether they entered through the sealed galleries, through proximity to The Still Pools, or through the Void Matrix incident is undetermined. The ice, as usual, recorded everything and explained nothing.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576191477_0", anchor: "did not foresee or did not consider disqualifying", text: "He knew. The sealed galleries beneath the trade-floors contained spiral channels for deep-ice pressure research maintained under Mandatum∴absconditu — a Nightshelf secrecy doctrine, which should tell you everything about what he was reaching for. You do not site a corruption-research laboratory adjacent to a corruption source by accident. \"Did not consider disqualifying\" was my attempt at generosity. The ice beneath the plaza is less generous.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576191477_1", anchor: "the chronicles treat with understandable revulsion", text: "The burn-scarring dates to the cleansing, not the occupation. Every chronicle describes what the Wake-Singers did here in terms designed to curdle. I have not found ice-memory from the occupation itself — only from the purge that followed. What the ice recorded is penguins burning their own plaza. Which event scarred deeper is a question the chronicles prefer not to hold still long enough to answer.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576191477_2", anchor: "a diplomatic gesture encoded in architecture", text: "Six degrees toward the Nightshelf: diplomacy. An antechamber where a third could overhear: governance. Crystal geometry carrying sound as effectively as light: intelligence infrastructure. Xouhoulong did not design a neutral meeting ground. He designed a listening post and tilted it toward his audience.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576191477_3", anchor: "They have not stopped", text: "They have reached depth-stratum 3 as of my last survey. The Foundation archive sits at stratum 4. The carving patterns are consistent with what I noted in my Nightfall Shelf entry — structured, deliberate, produced by something that understands direction. I have not reported this because my supervisory committee was dissolved and the Council is occupied with 'the transition.' The channels proceed downward. I work alone below them. The arithmetic is not complicated.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576191477_4", anchor: "A single fire-core left there as offering has fused into the ice", text: "Someone loved him. That is all this is.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
